# build output
dist/
dist-ssr/

# compiled contract artifacts
#
# The full PUBLIC Compact output of both eras is tracked, not just the module
# the frontend imports:
#
#   managed/<era>/contract/index.js|.d.ts|.js.map  — bundled into the frontend
#   managed/<era>/compiler/contract-info.json      — era/runtime declaration
#   managed/<era>/compiler/contract-manifest.json  — artifact integrity (v9)
#   managed/<era>/keys/*.verifier                  — circuit verifier keys
#   managed/<era>/keys/*.prover                    — circuit proving keys
#   managed/<era>/zkir/*.bzkir                     — circuit IR
#
# It is tracked because Vercel (and any other host) has no Compact toolchain
# and must not be asked to author contracts, yet the BROWSER fetches all of the
# above at runtime from this origin through FetchZkConfigProvider. Nothing in
# `managed/` is secret: a prover key is public circuit proving material, and
# the private data — the respondent's invite secret and the comment plaintext —
# is a runtime witness supplied inside the browser and never appears here. The
# real private state lives in `.admin-secret*`, `.participant-seed*` and the
# `.env` files, all of which stay ignored.
#
# `managed/<era>/zkir/*.zkir` is deliberately NOT required by the browser
# (FetchZkConfigProvider only requests `.bzkir`) but is tracked too, because
# `npm run compile` emits it and it is a few KB.
#
# Regenerate with `npm run compile:v9` / `npm run compile:v8`.

